\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs24\lang9 # Supplement Tracker App - Complete Specification\par
\par
## Project Overview\par
\par
**Purpose:** A self-experimentation/quantified-self app to study how supplements affect cognitive performance and physical symptoms through data correlation.\par
\par
**Core Philosophy:** Frictionless logging. Speed and simplicity over flashiness. Every interaction should be instant - no animations, no waiting, no fluff. If the user has to wait for loading or animations, the project has failed.\par
\par
**Target Platform:** Cross-platform mobile app (Android/iOS)\par
\par
**Development Approach:** Local storage initially, with CSV export for data analysis\par
\par
---\par
\par
## Core Features\par
\par
### 1. Home Screen\par
\par
**Layout:**\par
- 3 large buttons prominently displayed:\par
  - "Log Supplement"\par
  - "Log Symptom"  \par
  - "Cognitive Test"\par
- Small menu button (bottom corner)\par
- Small settings button (opposite bottom corner)\par
\par
**Design Requirements:**\par
- Instant boot time\par
- No background processes\par
- No ads\par
- Minimal, clean interface\par
\par
---\par
\par
### 2. Supplement Logging\par
\par
#### Supplement List View\par
\par
When "Log Supplement" is tapped, display a scrollable list of supplement buttons. Each button shows:\par
\par
- Small icon (customizable)\par
- Supplement name\par
- Standard/default dosage\par
- Color-changing clock icon (indicates if on schedule)\par
- Microscope icon (indicates if part of a cognitive study)\par
- Pencil icon (edit dosage/time taken)\par
- Plus icon at bottom (add new supplement)\par
\par
#### Logging Flow\par
\par
**When supplement button is tapped:**\par
1. Confirmation message displays for 10 seconds\par
2. During confirmation period, user can:\par
   - Tap "Home" to return to home screen\par
   - Tap "Edit" to modify or delete entry\par
   - Do nothing (auto-confirms after 10s)\par
   - Close app or sleep phone (auto-confirms)\par
3. Entry is logged with timestamp\par
\par
**Data Captured:**\par
- Supplement name\par
- Dosage amount\par
- Timestamp (second precision)\par
- Default: current time when button tapped\par
- User can edit actual time taken via edit icon\par
\par
**Design Philosophy:** Minimize taps and thinking for frequently repeated tasks. Default behavior should be correct 95% of the time.\par
\par
---\par
\par
### 3. Symptom Logging\par
\par
#### Body Diagram Interface\par
\par
Display interactive body diagram with tappable regions:\par
- Head\par
- Thorax\par
- Abdomen\par
- Pelvis\par
- Arms (left/right implied)\par
- Hands (left/right implied)\par
- Legs (left/right implied)\par
- Feet (left/right implied)\par
\par
#### Symptom Selection\par
\par
When region is tapped:\par
1. Display list of previously logged symptoms for that region\par
2. Show "Add New Custom Symptom" option\par
3. When symptom selected, capture:\par
   - **Severity scale:** 1-5 slider/buttons\par
   - **Notes field:** Optional text input\par
   - **Timestamp:** Second precision\par
\par
**Data Captured:**\par
- Body region\par
- Symptom description\par
- Severity (1-5)\par
- Notes (optional)\par
- Timestamp\par
\par
---\par
\par
### 4. Cognitive Tests\par
\par
Main cognitive test menu shows 4 options:\par
- "Reflexes"\par
- "Memory"\par
- "Judgment"\par
- "All 3"\par
\par
**Important:** Results have a 24-hour display delay to prevent gaming the system and learning effects.\par
\par
#### 4.1 Reflexes Test\par
\par
**Duration:** 10 seconds\par
\par
**Mechanics:**\par
- Small bubble (~1 cm diameter) appears at random location\par
- User taps bubble\par
- Bubble disappears, new bubble appears elsewhere\par
- Repeat until time expires\par
\par
**Scoring:**\par
- +1 point per successful tap\par
- -1 point per missed tap (tapping empty space)\par
- Track total score\par
\par
**Purpose:** Tests reaction time and hand-eye coordination. No learning curve - pure gut reaction.\par
\par
#### 4.2 Memory Test\par
\par
**Duration:** 60 seconds\par
\par
**Setup:**\par
- 48 cards in grid (6x8)\par
- 24 unique pairs\par
- Each card: 1 of 4 shapes (Triangle, Square, Circle, Cross) in 1 of 6 colors\par
- 4 shapes \'d7 6 colors = 24 combinations, each appearing twice\par
\par
**Game Flow:**\par
1. **Initial flash:** All cards shown face-up for 0.2 seconds\par
   - Purpose: Orientation aid, not memorization window\par
   - Too brief to scan specific pairs, gives general layout sense\par
2. All cards flip to blank\par
3. User taps first card \f1\u8594?\f0  reveals it\par
4. User taps second card \f1\u8594?\f0  reveals it\par
5. **If match:**\par
   - +2 points\par
   - Cards remain face-up\par
6. **If no match:**\par
   - -1 point\par
   - Cards flip back to blank\par
7. Repeat until all pairs found or timer expires\par
8. **End penalty:** -4 points per unpaired card\par
\par
**Design Note:** Wrong guesses still provide information about card locations. Test measures visual memory and pattern recognition under time pressure.\par
\par
#### 4.3 Judgment Test (Minimum Spanning Tree)\par
\par
**Duration:** 30 seconds\par
\par
**Setup:**\par
- 12 dots placed randomly on screen\par
- Dot placement algorithm:\par
  - Reject if within 1/6 screen width of another dot\par
  - Reject if within 1/12 screen width of edge\par
  - Ensures well-distributed dots, none too close\par
\par
**Objective:** Connect all dots into single network with minimum total line length\par
\par
**Controls:**\par
- **Add connection:** Drag between two dots OR tap two dots in sequence\par
- **Delete connection:** Tap two connected dots in sequence OR drag between already-connected dots\par
- When all dots connected into single network \f1\u8594?\f0  "Submit" button appears\par
\par
**Scoring:**\par
```\par
Base Score = (Optimal Solution Length / User Solution Length) \'d7 100\par
Rounded to nearest integer\par
```\par
\par
**Time Bonus (if score \f1\u8805?\f0  91):**\par
```\par
Bonus = [(Score - 90) \'d7 Seconds Remaining] / 5\par
Rounded to nearest integer\par
\par
Example: Score 93 with 17 seconds left\par
Bonus = [(93-90) \'d7 17] / 5 = 10 points\par
```\par
\par
**Purpose:** Tests spatial reasoning and optimization intuition. Infinite possible patterns prevent heuristic learning - pure gut judgment.\par
\par
---\par
\par
### 5. Supplement Management\par
\par
#### Edit Supplement (via Main Menu)\par
\par
**Immutable Fields:**\par
- Supplement name\par
- Dosage unit\par
\par
**Editable Fields:**\par
- Default dosage amount\par
- Icon\par
- Scheduling parameters\par
- Associated cognitive studies\par
\par
#### Scheduling System\par
\par
**Basic Reminders:**\par
- Set reminder time(s)\par
- Audible notification at scheduled time\par
- Custom repeat intervals\par
- Custom duration\par
- Multiple reminders per supplement allowed\par
  - Example: 7:00 AM and 1:00 PM daily\par
\par
**Exclusions & Warnings:**\par
Users can set safety rules:\par
- **Time-based:** "Do not take between XX:XX PM and YY:YY AM"\par
- **Dosage-based:** "Do not exceed X mg in Y hours"\par
\par
**Visual Indicators:**\par
- Clock icon turns **red** when exclusions active\par
- Warning displayed when user attempts to log during exclusion period\par
- User can override warning but is informed\par
\par
---\par
\par
### 6. Cognitive Study Protocols\par
\par
Users can associate cognitive tests with supplements to study effects.\par
\par
#### Study Types\par
\par
**Event-Based (Linked to Supplement Consumption):**\par
- Example: "Test memory every 5 minutes for 3 hours after taking Supplement X"\par
- Example: "Test judgment every hour for 8 hours after taking Supplement Y"\par
- Minimum interval: Test duration + 30 seconds\par
\par
**Schedule-Based (Daily Routine):**\par
- Example: "Test at wake, 1 hour after wake, noon, and 9:00 PM"\par
- Not linked to supplement consumption\par
\par
**Overlap Handling:**\par
- If two studies schedule tests within (test duration + 30s) interval\par
- Prompt user only once\par
- Data point counts as valid for both studies\par
- Prevents redundant testing\par
\par
---\par
\par
### 7. Sleep Tracking\par
\par
#### Automatic Detection\par
\par
**Mechanism:** Detect when phone becomes idle/active\par
\par
**Configuration:**\par
- User sets normal sleep time in settings\par
- Prevents false positives (e.g., leaving phone charging while working)\par
\par
**Data Captured:**\par
- Sleep start time\par
- Sleep end time  \par
- Duration\par
- Second precision\par
\par
#### Manual Override\par
\par
- User can review sleep log in main menu\par
- Edit entries as needed\par
- No manual "go to sleep now" button needed\par
\par
#### Sleep Reminders\par
\par
Two options:\par
1. **Time-based:** Alert at specific scheduled time\par
2. **Duration-based:** Alert X hours after last sleep (default: 16 hours)\par
\par
---\par
\par
## Data Architecture\par
\par
### Database Schema Requirements\par
\par
All timestamps use **second precision** for both supplements and symptoms.\par
\par
#### Supplements Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- name (unique)\par
- default_dosage (number)\par
- dosage_unit (text)\par
- icon_id (reference)\par
- schedule_enabled (boolean)\par
- study_enabled (boolean)\par
```\par
\par
#### Supplement_Logs Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- supplement_id (foreign key)\par
- timestamp (datetime, second precision)\par
- dosage (number)\par
- notes (text, optional)\par
```\par
\par
#### Symptoms Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- body_region (enum)\par
- description (text)\par
- last_used (datetime)\par
```\par
\par
#### Symptom_Logs Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- symptom_id (foreign key)\par
- timestamp (datetime, second precision)\par
- severity (integer, 1-5)\par
- notes (text, optional)\par
```\par
\par
#### Cognitive_Test_Results Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- test_type (enum: reflexes, memory, judgment)\par
- timestamp (datetime)\par
- score (integer)\par
- raw_data (json, test-specific metrics)\par
- study_id (foreign key, nullable)\par
- supplement_log_id (foreign key, nullable)\par
```\par
\par
#### Sleep_Logs Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- sleep_start (datetime)\par
- sleep_end (datetime)\par
- duration_seconds (integer)\par
- manually_edited (boolean)\par
```\par
\par
#### Schedules Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- supplement_id (foreign key)\par
- time (time)\par
- repeat_interval (text)\par
- enabled (boolean)\par
```\par
\par
#### Exclusions Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- supplement_id (foreign key)\par
- exclusion_type (enum: time_window, dosage_limit)\par
- parameters (json)\par
```\par
\par
#### Study_Protocols Table\par
```\par
- id (primary key)\par
- supplement_id (foreign key, nullable)\par
- test_type (enum)\par
- interval (integer, minutes)\par
- duration (integer, minutes)\par
- schedule_type (enum: event_based, daily_schedule)\par
- parameters (json)\par
```\par
\par
